<article class="env-lemma" id="0ED6">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0ED6">Lemma <span data-tag="0ED6">68.25.3</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a locally Noetherian and universally catenary scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$ such that $X$ is decent and such that the structure morphism $X \to S$ is locally of finite type. Then $X$ is catenary. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The question is local on $S$ (use Topology, Lemma <a href="/tag/02I2" data-tag="02I2">5.11.5</a>). Thus we may assume that $S$ has a dimension function, see Topology, Lemma <a href="/tag/02IC" data-tag="02IC">5.20.4</a>. Then we conclude that $|X|$ has a dimension function by Lemma <a href="/tag/0ED5" data-tag="0ED5">68.25.2</a>. Since $|X|$ is sober (Proposition <a href="/tag/03K6" data-tag="03K6">68.12.4</a>) we conclude that $|X|$ is catenary by Topology, Lemma <a href="/tag/02IA" data-tag="02IA">5.20.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>